\citation{horlacher2023}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces (a) Cross-protocol rank agreement between nested contributions before and after division by the headroom of the baseline, for each of the three protocol pairs in our data. Agreement improves in 3 of 3 pairs; only the GC-versus-dinucleotide improvement has a protein-clustered interval excluding zero. (b) The same test on the independent benchmark of Figure~\ref {fig:external}, $n=45$: rank agreement falls and disagreement rises under normalisation, the two criteria specified in advance as falsifying. The change in rank agreement is $-0.050$ ($-0.222$ to $+0.140$), a failure to replicate rather than a refutation.}}{11}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:recommendation}{{6}{11}{(a) Cross-protocol rank agreement between nested contributions before and after division by the headroom of the baseline, for each of the three protocol pairs in our data. Agreement improves in 3 of 3 pairs; only the GC-versus-dinucleotide improvement has a protein-clustered interval excluding zero. (b) The same test on the independent benchmark of Figure~\ref {fig:external}, $n=45$: rank agreement falls and disagreement rises under normalisation, the two criteria specified in advance as falsifying. The change in rank agreement is $-0.050$ ($-0.222$ to $+0.140$), a failure to replicate rather than a refutation}{figure.6}{}}
